---
description: Conventions for Drizzle schema, migrations, seeds, and Zod inference
alwaysApply: true
---

## Naming, casing, and mapping

- **Use camelCase in TypeScript schema definitions, snake_case in PostgreSQL**.
- **Map columns explicitly** when the DB name differs from the TS property:

```ts
// ✅ GOOD – camelCase fields mapped to snake_case columns
export const users = pgTable("users", {
  id: text("id").primaryKey(),
  email: text("email").notNull().unique(),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at")
    .defaultNow()
    .$onUpdate(() => new Date())
    .notNull(),
});
```

```ts
// ❌ AVOID – leaking camelCase directly to the DB without mapping
export const users = pgTable("users", {
  createdAt: timestamp("createdAt").defaultNow().notNull(),
});
```

## Timestamp conventions

- **Standardize timestamps as `createdAt` and `updatedAt` in TS**, mapped to `created_at` and `updated_at` in SQL.
- **Always use `.defaultNow()` and `.$onUpdate(() => new Date())`** on `updatedAt`:

```ts
export const posts = pgTable("posts", {
  id: text("id").primaryKey(),
  title: text("title").notNull(),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at")
    .defaultNow()
    .$onUpdate(() => new Date())
    .notNull(),
});
```

## Indexes and uniqueness

- **Always declare explicit indexes and unique constraints** in the table callback.
- **Name composite indexes** so they are easy to reference in migrations and DB tooling.

```ts
export const users = pgTable(
  "users",
  {
    id: text("id").primaryKey(),
    email: text("email").notNull().unique(),
    orgId: text("org_id").notNull(),
  },
  (table) => [index("idx_users_org_id").on(table.orgId)],
);
```

## Relations and many-to-many

- **Prefer Drizzle `relations()` for simple many-to-many** when the join table has no extra columns.
- **Use explicit join tables** when you need metadata or timestamps on the association:

```ts
export const userRoles = pgTable(
  "user_roles",
  {
    userId: text("user_id")
      .notNull()
      .references(() => users.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
    roleId: text("role_id")
      .notNull()
      .references(() => roles.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
    assignedAt: timestamp("assigned_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
  },
  (table) => [primaryKey({ columns: [table.userId, table.roleId] })],
);
```

## Enums

- **Prefer `pgEnum` over free-form strings** for constrained domains (status, role, provider, etc.).
- **Use SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE enum values** and map to snake_case in SQL when needed.

```ts
export const userStatus = pgEnum("user_status", ["ACTIVE", "INACTIVE", "SUSPENDED"]);

export const users = pgTable("users", {
  status: userStatus("status").default("ACTIVE").notNull(),
});
```

## Migrations

- **Use Drizzle Kit for schema changes** (`drizzle-kit generate` + `drizzle-kit migrate`).
- **Do not use `drizzle-kit push` for production** – it can drift from controlled, reviewed migrations.
- **Keep migration names descriptive and use snake_case** (e.g. `add_user_status_enum`, `add_organization_indexes`).
- **Avoid editing historical migrations** once applied to any shared environment; add new migrations instead.

## Seeds

- **Use idempotent seed scripts** that can be safely re-run.
- **Prefer upsert/onConflictDoUpdate over blind inserts** for reference data (roles, feature flags, default orgs).
- **Group seeding by domain** (users, roles, orgs) to keep scripts readable.

```ts
await db
  .insert(roles)
  .values({ id: "admin", name: "admin" })
  .onConflictDoUpdate({
    target: roles.name,
    set: { name: "admin" },
  });
```

## Zod schemas from Drizzle

- **Derive validation schemas from Drizzle tables with `drizzle-zod`** in `packages/db/src/validation/`, one file per domain (e.g. `validation/auth.ts`).
- Keep Drizzle table definitions in `packages/db/src/schema/` (e.g. `schema/auth.ts`).
- **Extend or pick fields in API domain `validation.ts` files** instead of duplicating column shapes by hand.

```ts
// packages/db/src/validation/auth.ts
import { createSelectSchema } from "drizzle-zod";
import { users } from "../schema/auth";

export const userSelectSchema = createSelectSchema(users);
export type User = z.infer<typeof userSelectSchema>;
```
